    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i just finished a rumenotomy on one of my dairy cows. can u give me a step by step on what i need to look out for regarding infection and how i should start her back on food? thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For post-rumenotomy care, you must watch for signs of infection like a fever, excessive discharge, or foul-smelling pus near the incision site. Keep the area clean and dry, and monitor her closely for any signs of systemic illness. When it comes to reintroducing feed, start with small amounts of easily digestible forage, like hay, and gradually increase the volume over several days. This slow reintroduction helps the rumen wall heal and prevents digestive upset, which is crucial after such a procedure. Remember to keep her comfortable and monitor her appetite closely during this entire recovery period.",
      "source": "target",
