      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Deep within the rumen, you are essentially looking for signs that the infection is becoming systemic, which is where the real danger lies. Since you can't see the internal workings, you must rely on the cow's overall health indicators, which are your best line of defense against internal trouble. Watch for lethargy, a sudden drop in appetite that persists beyond the normal post-op adjustment, or any signs of abdominal discomfort like reluctance to move or excessive rumination changes. If her general demeanor shifts from \"recovering\" to \"sick,\" it suggests the internal environment is becoming compromised, and a blood panel or ultrasound might be necessary to check for internal inflammation or infection.",
